{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: the new latch members' docs are two merged drafts**

Lines 2690-2696 stack two unrelated "Whether…" drafts on `reconfigureRefusedByAddFlow`:

- :2690-2692 describe the latch *state* ("Whether a provider add/connect flow is latched… Subclasses overriding [reconfigure] check this…") — that is `providerAddFlowInProgress`'s contract;
- :2693-2696 describe the *predicate* — the paragraph that actually matches the code.

Meanwhile `providerAddFlowInProgress` (this line and the next) carries a doc written in begin/end lifecycle semantics ("Marks an add-provider flow in progress: outside `reconfigure` calls are refused until [endProviderAddFlow]") rather than a getter description.

Proposed shape:

```dart
/// Whether a provider add/connect flow is latched (gh-1044 I1/AC6).
bool get providerAddFlowInProgress => _providerAddFlowDepth > 0;

/// Whether a `reconfigure` from outside an add-provider flow is currently
/// refused (the gh-1044 I1 latch): shared by the base [reconfigure] and
/// subclass overrides so the refusal rule exists in exactly one shape.
bool reconfigureRefusedByAddFlow(bool fromProviderAddFlow) =>
    _providerAddFlowDepth > 0 && !fromProviderAddFlow;
```

Doc-only, no behavior change.
